Z||000000||2xsess||12-04-2000||04:45 PM||||A little background first. I'm also on the Fiero mailing list and one day Rodney posted asking for someone to try out this new product he was thinking of making. Me being the kind gentleman that I am  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> offered to try it out. <BR>What this product does is make the power windows constantly hot so that you can roll them up and down with out having the key on. <BR>I received my trail one today. It's awesome, installed in less than 5 minutes with absolutely no cutting. <BR>I hope this isn't considered spam. I'm not really sure what everyone considers spam here. <BR>If you're interested they're only $6, I'm going to get some more of them for my van and one for my dad's Vette.  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Phil||12-04-2000||05:52 PM||||I rewired my windows to be hot all the time last spring, sure is handy not having to use the key whenever you want to use the windows.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||12-04-2000||07:03 PM||||I have rewired my windows on all my cars for the last 20+ years. I have many times told people how to do it. But there are a lot of people that just don't want to do it. Take the fuse box down and cut and splice wires. This is for those people. Easy to install. No wires to cut. Anyone can install this. ||||reg||1
